---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../../config';
---
<Base title="Reviews Policy | CQLocalPal" description="How reviews work here: tied to real completed orders, never bought or incentivised, never deleted for being negative, always answered.">
  <section>
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Reviews Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated: 4 November 2026 · v1.0</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>One rule above all</h2>
        <p>Every published review is tied to a completed, verifiable order. No exceptions, no "partner testimonials", no stock quotes.</p>
        <h2>How reviews are collected</h2>
        <p>After a service, each order gets exactly one invitation with a one-time link. Reviews are voluntary and <strong>never rewarded</strong> — no discounts, no gifts, no entries into anything. We never ask for screenshots of other platforms' reviews.</p>
        <h2>What we publish</h2>
        <p>Your rating, your words, a public nickname, and the month of service. We never publish order numbers, full dates, contact details, or anything that identifies your travel party.</p>
        <h2>What we never do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Delete or edit a negative review (we may reply, publicly)</li>
          <li>Buy reviews or outsource "reputation management"</li>
          <li>Gate low ratings behind waiting for our response</li>
          <li>Aggregate ratings we don't have — with zero reviews we show zero, not an invented average</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>If a review is false or abusive</h2>
        <p>Rare, but it happens: a review from someone who never travelled with us, or content that's unlawful. Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> with your order reference; a founder checks the order ledger and acts — including publishing a correction note when we got it wrong.</p>
        <h2>Referral incentives, disclosed</h2>
        <p>If we ever offer a discount for referring a friend, the review connected to it stays up with that fact attached. Incentives and honesty can coexist — as long as the incentive is visible.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
